      "message": "fix(motion): refuse a Ramp or Helix entry under control or wear compensation\n\nThe wall-side zig-zag of PR #3833, and the bore side's zig-zag, orbit and\ndive links, run on the lead-in and the ring before the lead-in move that\nengages G41/G42. Those moves post under G40 at the nominal centre, so a\nregister over the nominal radius, or a positive wear value, cut the wall.\ncontour_comp::door now refuses a Ramp or Helix entry or level transition\nunder control or wear compensation, by name. Computer compensation is\nunchanged.\n\nFixes #3888\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
